{"slug":"dot-star-pattern-match","title":"Does the Pattern With Dot and Star Match the Whole Text?","topic":"dp","difficulty":"hard","order":785,"tags":["dp","string","regex","pattern-matching"],"timeLimitMs":2000,"concept":{"title":"The star repeats the letter before it: skip the pair, or use it once more","body":["A tiny regular-expression matcher. In the pattern, a letter matches itself, a **dot** `.` matches any single letter, and a **star** `*` means \"**zero or more** of the element before it\" (the letter or the dot just in front of the star). The pattern must match the **whole** text. For the text `aab` and the pattern `c*a*b` the answer is yes (`c*` is empty, `a*` is `aa`, then `b`); for `mississippi` and `mis*is*p*.` it is no.","Let `ok(i, j)` be true if the first `i` letters of the text match the first `j` characters of the pattern. If the last pattern character `p[j]` is **not** a star, it must match one letter: `ok(i, j) = text[i] matches p[j] and ok(i - 1, j - 1)`. If it is a **star**, then `p[j-1]` is the element that repeats. Either it is used **zero times**, which removes the pair \"element + star\": `ok(i, j - 2)`; or it is used **once more**, which needs `text[i]` to match the element and the same pattern to match the shorter text: `ok(i - 1, j)`. So **`ok(i, j) = ok(i, j - 2) or (text[i] matches p[j-1] and ok(i - 1, j))`**.",{"code":"prev = [True] + [False] * m                          # the empty text\nfor j in range(2, m + 1):\n    if p[j - 1] == \"*\": prev[j] = prev[j - 2]        # x* can vanish\nfor i in range(1, n + 1):\n    cur = [False] * (m + 1)\n    for j in range(1, m + 1):\n        if p[j - 1] == \"*\":\n            cur[j] = cur[j - 2] or ((p[j - 2] == \".\" or p[j - 2] == t[i - 1]) and prev[j])\n        else:\n            cur[j] = (p[j - 1] == \".\" or p[j - 1] == t[i - 1]) and prev[j - 1]\n    prev = cur\nprint(\"yes\" if prev[m] else \"no\")"},"A direct recursive search may need exponential time on patterns such as `a*a*a*a*b` against `aaaa...a`, because the stars can share the letters in many ways. The table remembers each pair `(i, j)` once, so the time is O(n * m) and the memory O(m). The wildcard problem of the medium level had the same table with simpler star rules; here the star is tied to the element in front of it."]},"statement":["A text `t` and a pattern `p` are given. In the pattern a letter matches itself, `.` matches any single letter, and `*` means that the element in front of it (a letter or `.`) is repeated zero or more times. Print `yes` if the pattern matches the whole text, otherwise `no`."],"inputFormat":["The first line has the text `t` (lowercase letters).","The second line has the pattern `p` (lowercase letters, `.` and `*`)."],"outputFormat":["Print `yes` or `no`."],"constraints":["1 <= length of t <= 800","1 <= length of p <= 800","In the pattern every `*` follows a letter or a `.`."],"examples":[{"input":"aab\nc*a*b\n","output":"yes\n","note":"c* is empty, a* is aa, then b: yes."},{"input":"mississippi\nmis*is*p*.\n","output":"no\n","note":"The pattern cannot produce the whole text: no."}],"hints":["Let ok(i, j) say whether the first i letters of the text match the first j characters of the pattern.","A star can drop the pair (element, star): ok(i, j - 2), or consume one more letter: ok(i - 1, j) if the letter matches the element.","A dot matches any letter."],"starter":{"python":"import sys\ninput = sys.stdin.readline\n\nt = input().strip()\np = input().strip()\n\n# Your code here\n","cpp":"#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <string>\n#include <algorithm>\nusing namespace std;\n\nint main() {\n    ios::sync_with_stdio(false);\n    cin.tie(nullptr);\n\n    string t;\n    cin >> t;\n    string p;\n    cin >> p;\n\n    // Your code here\n\n    return 0;\n}\n","java":"import java.io.*;\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    static BufferedReader in = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));\n    static StringTokenizer tokens = new StringTokenizer(\"\");\n\n    static String next() throws IOException {\n        while (!tokens.hasMoreTokens()) {\n            tokens = new StringTokenizer(in.readLine());\n        }\n        return tokens.nextToken();\n    }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {\n        String t = next();\n        String p = next();\n\n        // Your code here\n    }\n}\n"},"solution":{"explanation":["ok(i, j) tells whether the first i letters of the text match the first j characters of the pattern: without a star at the end it needs a matching letter and ok(i - 1, j - 1); with a star after the element e it is ok(i, j - 2) (zero copies) or, if the letter matches e, ok(i - 1, j) (one more copy). Two rows are kept."],"complexity":"Time O(n * m), space O(m).","code":{"python":"import sys\ninput = sys.stdin.readline\n\nt = input().strip()\np = input().strip()\n\nn = len(t)\nm = len(p)\nprev = [True] + [False] * m\nfor j in range(2, m + 1):\n    if p[j - 1] == \"*\":\n        prev[j] = prev[j - 2]\nfor i in range(1, n + 1):\n    cur = [False] * (m + 1)\n    ti = t[i - 1]\n    for j in range(1, m + 1):\n        c = p[j - 1]\n        if c == \"*\":\n            e = p[j - 2]\n            cur[j] = cur[j - 2] or ((e == \".\" or e == ti) and prev[j])\n        else:\n            cur[j] = (c == \".\" or c == ti) and prev[j - 1]\n    prev = cur\nprint(\"yes\" if prev[m] else \"no\")\n","cpp":"#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <string>\n#include <algorithm>\nusing namespace std;\n\nint main() {\n    ios::sync_with_stdio(false);\n    cin.tie(nullptr);\n\n    string t;\n    cin >> t;\n    string p;\n    cin >> p;\n\n    int n = (int)t.size(), m = (int)p.size();\n    vector<char> prev(m + 1, 0), cur(m + 1, 0);\n    prev[0] = 1;\n    for (int j = 2; j <= m; j++) if (p[j - 1] == '*') prev[j] = prev[j - 2];\n    for (int i = 1; i <= n; i++) {\n        fill(cur.begin(), cur.end(), 0);\n        for (int j = 1; j <= m; j++) {\n            char c = p[j - 1];\n            if (c == '*') {\n                char e = p[j - 2];\n                cur[j] = cur[j - 2] || ((e == '.' || e == t[i - 1]) && prev[j]);\n            } else {\n                cur[j] = (c == '.' || c == t[i - 1]) && prev[j - 1];\n            }\n        }\n        swap(prev, cur);\n    }\n    cout << (prev[m] ? \"yes\" : \"no\") << \"\\n\";\n\n    return 0;\n}\n","java":"import java.io.*;\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    static BufferedReader in = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));\n    static StringTokenizer tokens = new StringTokenizer(\"\");\n\n    static String next() throws IOException {\n        while (!tokens.hasMoreTokens()) {\n            tokens = new StringTokenizer(in.readLine());\n        }\n        return tokens.nextToken();\n    }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {\n        String t = next();\n        String p = next();\n\n        int n = t.length(), m = p.length();\n        boolean[] prev = new boolean[m + 1];\n        boolean[] cur = new boolean[m + 1];\n        prev[0] = true;\n        for (int j = 2; j <= m; j++) if (p.charAt(j - 1) == '*') prev[j] = prev[j - 2];\n        for (int i = 1; i <= n; i++) {\n            Arrays.fill(cur, false);\n            for (int j = 1; j <= m; j++) {\n                char c = p.charAt(j - 1);\n                if (c == '*') {\n                    char e = p.charAt(j - 2);\n                    cur[j] = cur[j - 2] || ((e == '.' || e == t.charAt(i - 1)) && prev[j]);\n                } else {\n                    cur[j] = (c == '.' || c == t.charAt(i - 1)) && prev[j - 1];\n                }\n            }\n            boolean[] swap = prev;\n            prev = cur;\n            cur = swap;\n        }\n        System.out.println(prev[m] ? \"yes\" : \"no\");\n    }\n}\n"}},"tests":[{"input":"aab\nc*a*b\n","output":"yes\n"},{"input":"mississippi\nmis*is*p*.\n","output":"no\n"},{"input":"a\na*\n","output":"yes\n"},{"input":"a\n.*\n","output":"yes\n"},{"input":"ab\n.*c\n","output":"no\n"},{"input":"aaa\na*a\n","output":"yes\n"},{"input":"aabaaabaaaaaababbbab\nb*abb.*baab*\n","output":"no\n"},{"input":"babaaaaaabaabaaaaaababbbababbbaaabababaabbabaababbbbaaabbbaabaaaabababbaaaabbabaaabaababaaaaaabbaaab\nbbaa*a*a*aab.*bbaa*bb*b*b*ab.*bab*a*a*bbb*aa.a*bba*a*aaaa*.a\n","output":"no\n"},{"input":"\na*bb*bcacbba.*c*aaab*c*c*ba.*a*c*a*ac*c*bcbbc*a*bba*bcc*c*bab*b*ccbbba*a*bcc.*c*caca*a.cba*cbbaba*abc*cb*c*ccbbaacc*bbb.babb.c*acc*b*b*a*a*bab*a.*.ab*a*bccb*c*c*bca*b*.*c*ccbcc.c*ba*..cb.ccab*cb*bcbc*\n","output":"no\n"},{"input":"\na*a*babab.*b*a*b*.*b*..*a*b*b*bab*ba*a.*b*baabb*a*ba*aa*b*ba*b.*aa*a*a*aabaab*baaba*a.*bb*a*b*b*ba*aa*b*a*bab*.*bbb*b*baa*b*bab*b*a*a*a*aa*a*b*a*baab*b.aa*b*bb*bb*b*a*b*b*bbabbaabb*ab*.abb*b*aa*bbb*a*ab*b*.b.*bbb*b*a*..a*b*b.b*ba*a*b*aba*baa.*.*.*a*a*ab*aab*a*bb*a*aaab*ab*aa*bb*ab*.b*a*aba*ba*aabaa*a*ab*a.*a*bb.*.*b*a*bb*a*a*ba*a*b.*a*ba*b*ba*bbbb*b*b*aabab*.*b*ab*b*a.*b*b*bb*b*a*.bb*a*aa.*b*a*aa*b*.b*ab*b*aabb*a*bbb*.bbab*.*b*a*b*baa*bba*bab*aaa*a*a*aa*baa.*b*baaaa*ba*ba*.bbbbaa*b*a*a*ab*b*b*babb*bb*ba*bbb*.aaa*b*ab*a*a*a*b*aa*.*bb*ba.*ab*aba*b*a*b*a*a*b*b*a*b*b*.*abaabb*b.*.*a*.*baba*bbbbbb*a*aa*bb*abaa*b*b*a*a*baabab*.*a*bbb*baa*abbbb*bbabb*.*b*ab*a*a*a.*ba*.a*a*b*a*a*bab*b*aaaab*bb*b*ab*b*abab*a*.*b*bab*a*a*a*b*b.*baa*b*bb*b.*.b*b*bb*aa*a*ba*.*ba*bb*a*abaababb*bab*.*bb*aaab*aa*aa*aba*a\n","output":"no\n"},{"input":"\na*a*a*a*aaa*a*a*a*aa*aa*a*a*a*..aa*aa*aaa*a*aaaaa*a.*a*aa*aaaa*aaaa*a.a*aa.a*a*aa*a*a*.aaaa*a*aa*aa*a*a*aaa*aa*a*aa*a*a*a*a*a*aa*a*aa*aa*aaa*a.aaa*aaa*a*aa*aa.*a*aaa*a*a*aaaa*a*a*a*aa*a*a*aaa*aa.*a*aa*a*aa*a*a*aaa*aaa*aa*a*a*a*aa*aaa*aa*a*aa.aa*a*a*.aa*a*a*a*aaa*.*a*aaa*aaaa*a*aa.a*aa*aaaaa*aaa*aa*aa*a*aaaaa*aa*.*aaa*aaa*a*a*a*aa*.*aaaa*.*aaaa*aa*aa*a*aa*aa*aaaa*aa*a*aa*a*aa*a*a.*.*aaaaaaaaaa*a*aa\n","output":"yes\n"},{"input":"\naa*aa*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*aa*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*aa*a*a*a*aa*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*aaa*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*aa*a*a*a*aa*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*aa*a*a*a*aaa*a*a*a*a*aa*aa*a*a*a*a*a*a*aa*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*aa*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*aaa*aa*a*aa*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*aa*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*aa*a*a*a*a*a*a*aa*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*aa*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*aa*a*a*a*aa*a*a*aa*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*aa*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*aa*a*a*aa*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*aaa*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*aa*a*a*a*a*aa*a*a*a*aa*a*aa*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*aa*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*aa*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*aaa*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*a*aa*a*a\n","output":"yes\n"},{"input":"\nb*a*a*.abbaaca.*a*a.baccaabc.ba.a*..*a*.bbacb.*ca.*b*bab*.b.acab*cca*.*.a*..*b*c.a*.b.*abb*bcb*.bbcb*abaab*bb*.aa*bc*.c*.c.a*b.*b*bc*.*bb*aa..ab*b.cab.*bbbc*a.*.aa*b*cccacc*c.a*ca..*..*aa.ca*.*.*a*.bcb*cb*a*baaababc*.*.*.a*ba*.b*.abcbcb*bc.*aac*a.bac*..*b*ca.c*cab*.bab*a.b...a..*a*.*b..a*c.*ba*b*a.*a.*.b*c.b*b.ac..b*a.caca.aaac..*.aa.a.*a*c..cba*c*cc*c*aaa.*..ac*a.*.*.ba*a.*aaba.*ab.*a*caca*c*baa..b*b.a*c*.*b.c*..a.c.c*.cb*..c.a*aa.a*ca*baacc*c*a*cc..cc*caba.ba*.acaab*.*ccb*aab*ca.a.*a..*c*b..ab*bcbac.acb*.bc..a*.*babb*caac*.b.c.*.ccacb*.b*ac.bcc..a*a.ab*b..bbcc*cbcb..*bca*bbcb.*a.*ab.a.baa*b.\n","output":"no\n"},{"input":"\nbb*bb.ba.aaab*b.b*b*babab*.*aaaaaaaa*.*abb*aaaabb*b*aabb*aa*aba*baa*.aab.*a*b*ababbbb*aabb*a..abb*bb*a*bb*bb.b*a*a.a*ab*aba*a*a.a*.a*aa*a*..*b*abab*a.a*a*aa*ba*b*aaaa*a*a*ba.a*bbbaa*.*bab*.aa*b.a.aaa*.b*.aba*.*a*a*a*.*a*abb*ba*ab*..*abb*bbaa*a*aa*aa*b*a.*aa*abb*bb.aba*b.aba*b*.ba*.b*.*b*aba*.bb*b*ab*.*abba*b*.*b*.*.b*a.*aa*aa*ab*ab*b*b*a*abb*b*ab.*b*aabab*..*a.*b*a.a*b*b*abb*bbb*.*a*a*b..*aa.b*b*b*a*b*baa*baaaa.a*b*aa*b*ab*b*ba.b*b.aa*aaba*b*.b*ba*a*.abb*aaa*b.*a*aaaaab*a*a*b.ab.ab*.*.*a.bba*.*ababa*.bbaa*a*.*ab.*.a*aabab*abbb*..bbbb*a*ba*a*b.*a*aab.*ba*b*.*.*b..ba.*b*a*a*ba.abb.*b*b*bbbbab*b*baaba*ba*b*b*ba.*.*.abbba*a.b.*..*a*b*ba*.abbb*b*.*b*b*.*b*a*.*a*.a*a*.*abaaabbbaaab*b*